From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohan Garg <rohan@rsntl.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 01:30:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nir: derive color_is_dual_source from declared vars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

color_is_dual_source was only set when a store to the index=1
(or FRAG_RESULT_DUAL_SRC_BLEND) output survived to gather_info.
nir_opt_undef removes stores of entirely-undef values, so a
shader assigning undef to its second output lost the flag even
though the interface still declares it.

Derive the flag from declared output variables instead, so it
reflects the interface regardless of whether a store survived.
Drop the now-subsumed store-gated check in set_io_mask().

Fixes: 175e1f3cf534 ("nir: Set info->fs.color_is_dual_source for DUAL_SRC_BLEND var locations")
Signed-off-by: Rohan Garg <rohan@rsntl.com>
Reviewed-by: Marek Olšák <maraeo@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit ad3f9856e08d75ea44e46e6a3782633ce2d7da42)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44489>
(cherry picked from commit 3496dd01e82039a2a75f2ee655b7fa066a7d428d)
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_gather_info.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_gather_info.c b/src/compiler/nir/nir_gather_info.c
index b625b1f6414..6f37f1b4ecd 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_gather_info.c
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_gather_info.c
@@ -198,11 +198,6 @@ set_io_mask(nir_shader *shader, nir_variable *var, int offset, int len,
             }
          }
 
-         if (shader->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT && !is_output_read &&
-             (var->data.index == 1 ||
-              var->data.location == FRAG_RESULT_DUAL_SRC_BLEND))
-            shader->info.fs.color_is_dual_source = true;
-
          if (var->data.per_view)
             shader->info.per_view_outputs |= bitfield;
       }
@@ -1166,6 +1161,18 @@ nir_shader_gather_info(nir_shader *shader, nir_function_impl *entrypoint)
             glsl_count_attribute_slots(glsl_get_array_element(var->type), false);
          shader->info.per_view_outputs |= BITFIELD64_RANGE(var->data.location, slots);
       }
+
+      /*
+       * Dual-source blending is part of the shader interface, not a
+       * property of whether the output ends up written: a var with
+       * index == 1 still selects dual-source blending even if every
+       * store to it got optimized away (e.g. nir_opt_undef removing a
+       * store whose value is entirely undef).
+       */
+      shader->info.fs.color_is_dual_source |=
+         shader->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT &&
+         (var->data.index == 1 ||
+          var->data.location == FRAG_RESULT_DUAL_SRC_BLEND);
    }
 
    if (shader->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_FRAGMENT) {
-- 
